      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MiniMax H3 + Spectrum — Ref2VA MAXIMUM INPUT WORKFLOW\n\n## Every native reference socket is exposed and connected\n- **9 reference pictures**\n- **3 reference videos**\n- **3 paired video soundtracks** extracted from those videos\n- **3 standalone audio references**\n\n## Use\n1. Replace every placeholder picture, video and audio file you intend to use.\n2. Respect the model's documented combined limit of 12 uploaded files; leave unnecessary references out of the actual run.\n3. Reference inputs with exact tags: `<Picture N>`, `<Video N>`, `<Audio N>`.\n4. Give each reference one explicit job: identity, wardrobe, prop, environment, style, motion, camera, voice, music or ambience.\n5. Use 24 fps reference videos where possible. Ref videos and audio are documented for 2–15 s, with 15 s total per media type.\n\n## Memory / quality\n- `ref_image_size = match` is deliberately the safe default.\n- `max` retains up to a 2048 px short edge and can become several times slower because reference tokens remain active at every denoising step. With many pictures it can also explode RAM/VRAM use.\n- Start at 0.4 MP / 5 s; then increase one variable at a time.\n- Spectrum is enabled with the conservative preset. Disable it and keep the seed fixed for a reference-fidelity A/B comparison.\n\n## Local models\n- Diffusion: `MiniMax H3\\minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n- Text Encoder: `MiniMax H3\\qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n- Video VAE: `MiniMax H3\\minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors`\n- Audio VAE: `MiniMax H3\\minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors`\n"
      ],
      "title": "README — Ref2VA MAXIMUM / ALL NATIVE REFERENCE SOCKETS",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
