      "widgets_values": [
        "REFERENCE MAP — delete every unused line before rendering.\n\nUse <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>, and <Picture 3> as complementary identity views of the main subject; preserve facial structure, body proportions, age, skin detail, hair, and distinctive features.\nUse <Picture 4> as the exact wardrobe and accessory reference.\nUse <Picture 5> as the environment and set-layout reference.\nUse <Picture 6> as the lighting, color palette, and exposure reference.\nUse <Picture 7> as the hero prop or object-design reference.\nUse <Picture 8> as the material, texture, and close-detail reference.\nUse <Picture 9> as the final composition and overall visual-style reference.\n\nUse <Video 1> for the main subject's performance, pose progression, body motion, timing, and facial movement.\nUse <Video 2> for camera path, lens behavior, framing, focus pulls, and shot rhythm.\nUse <Video 3> for secondary motion, environmental dynamics, cloth or hair motion, and transition timing.\n\nAssuming all three videos contain soundtracks: use <Audio 1>, <Audio 2>, and <Audio 3> only for the paired timing/voice/SFX information carried by Videos 1–3. Use standalone <Audio 4> as the primary voice reference, <Audio 5> as music/rhythm reference, and <Audio 6> as ambience/Foley reference. If any video is silent, renumber the later Audio tags according to the TAG MAP note.\n\nGenerate a new coherent cinematic shot rather than copying pixels. Preserve the assigned identities, wardrobe, props, environment, materials, lighting, and style while following the assigned motion and camera references. Keep anatomy stable and temporal continuity clean. No duplicate subjects, no identity swaps, no unrequested cuts, no abrupt morphs, no disappearing props, and no contradictory camera motion. Generate synchronized native stereo audio appropriate to the new scene."
      ],
      "title": "PROMPT — ALL PICTURE / VIDEO / AUDIO TAGS",
