      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# TAG MAP — IMPORTANT\n\nThe conditioning presentation is ordered as follows:\n1. Pictures first: `<Picture 1>` … `<Picture 9>`\n2. Then each video. If that video contains audio, its paired `<Audio N>` is inserted immediately before its `<Video N>` token.\n3. Standalone audio references come last.\n\nWith three videos that all contain soundtracks:\n- Video 1 soundtrack = `<Audio 1>`\n- Video 2 soundtrack = `<Audio 2>`\n- Video 3 soundtrack = `<Audio 3>`\n- Standalone Audio 1 = `<Audio 4>`\n- Standalone Audio 2 = `<Audio 5>`\n- Standalone Audio 3 = `<Audio 6>`\n\nIf one reference video is silent, that paired audio tag is omitted and every later audio ordinal shifts down. Therefore remove or rename the affected `<Audio N>` lines in the prompt.\n\n## Documented mixed-input limit\nThe graph exposes every native socket, but H3 documents a maximum of **12 uploaded files total**. Do not normally run all 9 picture files + 3 video files + 3 standalone audio files together. Valid maximum examples:\n- 9 pictures + 3 videos = 12 files\n- 6 pictures + 3 videos + 3 standalone audios = 12 files\n- 9 pictures + 3 standalone audios = 12 files\n\nThe soundtracks embedded in the three video files are paired through `Get Video Components`; they are not separate uploads.\n"
      ],
      "title": "REFERENCE TAG ORDER + 12-FILE LIMIT",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
